#: frontend/src/pages/PersonalDevelopmentPlan.vue:152
#: seminary/public/frontend/assets/PersonalDevelopmentPlan-BahtR62c.js:2
msgid "How I will go about it"
msgstr "Cómo lo abordaré"

#. Label of the testimony (Long Text) field in DocType 'Student Applicant'
#. Label of a field in the student-applicant Web Form
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/student_applicant/student_applicant.json
#: seminary/seminary/web_form/student_applicant/student_applicant.json
msgid "How did you become a believer? What changed in your life?"
msgstr "¿Cómo te has convertido en un creyente? ¿Qué cambió en tu vida?"

#. Description of the 'Distance Unit' (Select) field in DocType 'Seminary
#. Settings'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/seminary_settings/seminary_settings.json
msgid "How distances are shown when the Cohort Planner reports how far a student lives from a mentor. One setting for the whole school, so a plan reads the same way to everyone who opens it."
msgstr ""
"Cómo se muestran las distancias cuando el Planificador de cohortes informa "
"de la distancia entre la residencia de un estudiante y la de un mentor. Es "
"una configuración para toda la institución, de modo que el plan se lea de la "
"misma manera para todas las personas que lo abran."

#. Label of the pgmexpect (Long Text) field in DocType 'Student Applicant'
#. Label of a field in the student-applicant Web Form
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/student_applicant/student_applicant.json
#: seminary/seminary/web_form/student_applicant/student_applicant.json
msgid "How enrolling in this program will help you serve the church?"
msgstr "¿Cómo inscribirse en este programa le ayudará a servir la Iglesia?"

#. Description of the 'Faculty read scope' (Select) field in DocType 'Seminary
#. Settings'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/seminary_settings/seminary_settings.json
msgid "How far an instructor of record can see beyond the sections they teach. School: every section. Academic Unit: only sections of courses owned by an academic unit they belong to (their department, its parent units, and interdepartments it constitutes). Courses with no academic unit, and instructors with no unit membership, are treated as School. Graders and assistants only ever see their own sections."
msgstr ""
"Hasta dónde puede ver un docente responsable más allá de las secciones que "
"imparte. Facultad: todas las secciones. Unidad académica: solo las secciones "
"de cursos pertenecientes a una unidad académica a la que pertenece (su "
"departamento, las unidades superiores de este y los interdepartamentos que "
"constituye). Los cursos sin unidad académica y los docentes sin pertenencia "
"a una unidad se consideran pertenecientes a la Facultad. Los calificadores y "
"asistentes solo pueden ver sus propias secciones."

#: frontend/src/pages/AlumniProfile.vue:118
#: seminary/public/frontend/assets/AlumniProfile-D4TdFPKe.js:1
msgid "How is this different from my message preferences?"
msgstr "¿En qué se diferencia esto de mis preferencias de mensajes?"

#. Description of the 'Hours Tracking' (Select) field in DocType 'Internship
#. Type'
#: seminary/partner/doctype/internship_type/internship_type.json
msgid "How logged hours count toward the total. 'Portal Daily Log' counts immediately; '... with Supervisor Confirmation' counts only verified rows; 'Submittable Log' counts once the designated hour-log requirement is signed complete."
msgstr ""
"Cómo se contabilizan las horas registradas para el total. «Portal Daily Log» "
"se contabiliza de inmediato; «... with Supervisor Confirmation» solo "
"contabiliza las filas verificadas; «Submittable Log» se contabiliza una vez "
"que el requisito de registro de horas designado se haya firmado como "
"completado."

#. Description of the 'Tardies per Absence' (Int) field in DocType 'Seminary
#. Settings'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/seminary_settings/seminary_settings.json
msgid "How many Tardies count as one Absence toward the limit (e.g. 3 → every 3 tardies add 1 absence). Set to 0 to disable tardy-to-absence conversion."
msgstr ""
"¿Cuántas tardanzas cuentan como una ausencia para el límite (p. ej., 3 → "
"cada 3 tardanzas añaden 1 ausencia)? Establezca el valor en 0 para "
"desactivar la conversión de tardanzas en ausencias."

#. Description of the 'Attendance Policy' (Section Break) field in DocType
#. 'Course Schedule'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/course_schedule/course_schedule.json
msgid "How many class meetings a student may miss before being flagged at risk of failing for absences. Editable only by the registrar / Program Chair."
msgstr ""
"Número de clases que un estudiante puede faltar antes de ser marcado en "
"riesgo de suspender por inasistencias. Editable solo por secretaría / "
"director del programa."

#. Description of the 'Cohorts Per Member' (Int) field in DocType 'Cohort Type'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/cohort_type/cohort_type.json
msgid "How many cohorts of this type one person may belong to at once (0 = any number). A cohort and everything split off from it count as one, so a group that multiplies is still the one commitment its members made. Usually 1: being mentored in two places at once is rarely what a school means, and it is how one leader would otherwise gather far more people than the size limit suggests. Existing memberships are never broken by lowering this -- it applies as people are added."
msgstr ""
"Cuántas cohortes de este tipo puede integrar una persona a la vez (0 = "
"cualquier cantidad). Una cohorte y todo lo que se deriva de ella cuentan "
"como una sola, por lo que un grupo que se multiplica sigue siendo el único "
"compromiso que asumieron sus miembros. Por lo general, 1: que una persona "
"reciba mentoría en dos lugares a la vez rara vez es lo que una institución "
"educativa pretende, y de otro modo permitiría que un líder reuniera a muchas "
"más personas de lo que sugiere el límite de tamaño. Las membresías "
"existentes nunca se cancelan al reducir este límite; se aplica a medida que "
"se agregan personas."

#. Description of the 'Activity Grading Mode' (Select) field in DocType
#. 'Competency Framework'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/competency_framework/competency_framework.json
msgid "How many grades an activity collects."
msgstr "Cuántas calificaciones recopila una actividad."

#. Description of the 'Quantity Required' (Int) field in DocType 'Program Grad
#. Req Items'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/program_grad_req_items/program_grad_req_items.json
msgid "How many instances the student must satisfy. Only meaningful for Manual Verification (e.g. '8 chapel attendances'). Event Attendance and Linked Document always count as 1."
msgstr "Cuántas instancias el estudiante debe satisfacer. Sólo significativo para la verificación manual (por ejemplo, '8 asistencias al capítulo'). La asistencia al evento y el documento vinculado siempre cuentan como 1."

#. Description of the 'Chapel Check-in Closes After (mins)' (Int) field in
#. DocType 'Seminary Settings'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/seminary_settings/seminary_settings.json
msgid "How many minutes after a chapel's end time (or start, if no end) students may still self check-in. Set both this and 'opens before' to 0 to disable the time window entirely."
msgstr ""
"Cuántos minutos después de la hora de finalización de una capilla (o de "
"inicio, si no tiene hora de finalización) los estudiantes todavía pueden "
"registrarse por sí mismos. Establezca tanto esta opción como «se abre antes» "
"en 0 para desactivar por completo la ventana de tiempo."

#. Description of the 'Check-in Closes After (mins)' (Int) field in DocType
#. 'Seminary Settings'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/seminary_settings/seminary_settings.json
msgid "How many minutes after a meeting's end time (or start, if no end) students may still self check-in."
msgstr ""
"Cuántos minutos después de la hora de finalización de una reunión (o de "
"inicio, si no tiene hora de finalización) los estudiantes todavía pueden "
"registrarse por sí mismos."

#. Description of the 'Chapel Check-in Opens Before (mins)' (Int) field in
#. DocType 'Seminary Settings'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/seminary_settings/seminary_settings.json
msgid "How many minutes before a chapel's start time students may begin self check-in. Set both this and 'closes after' to 0 to disable the time window entirely (check-in allowed any time while the chapel is confirmed)."
msgstr ""
"Cuántos minutos antes de la hora de inicio de una capilla pueden los "
"estudiantes comenzar el registro automático. Establezca tanto esto como «se "
"cierra después de» en 0 para desactivar por completo la ventana de tiempo "
"(se permite el registro en cualquier momento mientras la capilla esté "
"confirmada)."

#. Description of the 'Check-in Opens Before (mins)' (Int) field in DocType
#. 'Seminary Settings'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/seminary_settings/seminary_settings.json
msgid "How many minutes before a meeting's start time students may begin self check-in."
msgstr ""
"Cuántos minutos antes de la hora de inicio de una reunión pueden los "
"estudiantes comenzar a registrarse por sí mismos."

#. Description of the 'Readers Required' (Int) field in DocType 'Culminating
#. Project Type'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/culminating_project_type/culminating_project_type.json
msgid "How many named readers (beyond the advisor) this project carries. A project has at most two (Second and Third Reader); put any further reviewers on the committee."
msgstr ""
"Cuántos lectores designados, además del asesor, participan en este proyecto. "
"Un proyecto admite como máximo dos (segundo y tercer lector); asigne "
"cualquier revisor adicional al comité."

#. Description of the 'Results Per Page' (Int) field in DocType 'Pexels
#. Settings'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/pexels_settings/pexels_settings.json
msgid "How many photos to fetch per search page (1-80)."
msgstr "Cuántas fotos obtener por página de búsqueda (1-80)."

#. Description of the 'Maximum Planned Cohort Size' (Int) field in DocType
#. 'Cohort Type'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/cohort_type/cohort_type.json
msgid "How many students one proposed cohort may hold. The planner decides how many cohorts to open from this and the minimum above, before it places anybody. 0 = no ceiling."
msgstr ""
"Cuántos estudiantes puede admitir una cohorte propuesta. El planificador "
"decide cuántas cohortes abrir a partir de este valor y del mínimo indicado "
"arriba, antes de asignar a nadie. 0 = sin límite superior."

#. Description of the 'Words to Hide' (Int) field in DocType 'Question'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/question/question.json
msgid "How many words to hide for the student to fill in."
msgstr "Cuántas palabras ocultar para que el estudiante las complete."

#. Description of the 'Content Release' (Section Break) field in DocType
#. 'Competency Framework'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/competency_framework/competency_framework.json
msgid "How much of a course a student can see before reflecting on what came before."
msgstr ""
"Qué parte de un curso puede ver un estudiante antes de reflexionar sobre lo "
"visto anteriormente."

#. Description of a DocType
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/assessment_dimension_weight/assessment_dimension_weight.json
msgid "How much one graded activity counts toward one dimension of its competency. Weights are relative, so 60/20/20 and 3/1/1 behave the same, and 0 means the activity does not measure that dimension."
msgstr ""
"Cuánto cuenta una actividad evaluada para una dimensión de su competencia. "
"Las ponderaciones son relativas, por lo que 60/20/20 y 3/1/1 funcionan "
"igual, y 0 significa que la actividad no mide esa dimensión."

#: frontend/src/pages/CourseAssessment.vue:167
#: seminary/public/frontend/assets/CourseAssessment-4OpsOBdH.js:4
msgid "How much this assessment says about each dimension. Leave them equal if it says the same about all."
msgstr ""
"Cuánto indica esta evaluación sobre cada dimensión. Déjelas iguales si "
"indica lo mismo sobre todas."

#: frontend/src/pages/CourseForm.vue:159
#: seminary/public/frontend/assets/CourseForm-COfUeHIE.js:4
msgid "How students reach the content"
msgstr "Cómo acceden los estudiantes al contenido"

#. Description of the 'Evaluation Model' (Select) field in DocType 'Internship
#. Type'
#: seminary/partner/doctype/internship_type/internship_type.json
msgid "How the internship is graded. 'Inherited from Course' requires a backing course (the course's grading scale applies). Without a course, pick Pass/Fail or Graded; the faculty advisor records the outcome on the application."
msgstr ""
"Cómo se califica la práctica profesional. «Heredado del curso» requiere un "
"curso asociado (se aplica la escala de calificaciones del curso). Sin un "
"curso, seleccione Aprobado/Suspenso o Calificado; el asesor académico "
"registra el resultado en la solicitud."

#. Description of the 'Phonetic Name' (Data) field in DocType 'Person'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/person/person.json
msgid "How the name should be pronounced (e.g. 'JOH-ann mar-TEEN-ess'). Used for ceremony and roll calls."
msgstr ""
"Cómo debe pronunciarse el nombre (p. ej., «JOH-ann mar-TEEN-ess»). Se "
"utiliza para las ceremonias y la lectura de nombres."

#. Description of the 'Matching Rules' (Table) field in DocType 'Cohort Type'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/cohort_type/cohort_type.json
msgid "How the planner decides who mentors whom. Leave empty and it balances group sizes only. Filters narrow who may be paired; Rankings order the mentors who qualify, the first listed deciding and the next breaking its ties. Whatever it proposes, a person reviews and can override it."
msgstr ""
"Así decide el planificador quién asesora a quién. Déjelo vacío y solo "
"equilibrará el tamaño de los grupos. Los filtros limitan quién puede formar "
"pareja; las clasificaciones ordenan a los mentores que cumplen los "
"requisitos: la primera determina el orden y la siguiente desempata. Sea cual "
"sea su propuesta, una persona la revisa y puede anularla."

#. Description of the 'Competency Verdict' (Section Break) field in DocType
#. 'Competency Framework'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/competency_framework/competency_framework.json
msgid "How the separate ratings become one result per competency."
msgstr ""
"Cómo las calificaciones independientes se convierten en un resultado por "
"competencia."

#: frontend/src/pages/CompetencyGradebook.vue:275
#: seminary/public/frontend/assets/CompetencyGradebook-DOQtHgLX.js:3
msgid "How this is demonstrated"
msgstr "Cómo se demuestra esto"

#. Description of the 'Placed By' (Small Text) field in DocType 'Cohort
#. Membership'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/cohort_membership/cohort_membership.json
msgid "How this person came to be in this cohort. Filled by the Cohort Planner: either the rules that proposed the pairing, or a note that somebody moved them by hand while reviewing. It records a decision and changes nothing."
msgstr ""
"Cómo llegó esta persona a formar parte de esta cohorte. Lo completa el "
"Planificador de cohortes: las reglas que propusieron la asignación o una "
"nota que indica que alguien la cambió manualmente durante la revisión. "
"Registra una decisión y no cambia nada."

#. Description of the 'Relation' (Select) field in DocType 'Cohort Post Link'
#: seminary/seminary/doctype/cohort_post_link/cohort_post_link.json
msgid "How this post relates to the linked one."
msgstr "Cómo se relaciona esta publicación con la vinculada."

#: frontend/src/pages/CourseCalendar.vue:25
